# Ansible Infrastructure Lab

A hands-on Ansible project for automating the configuration and management of Linux servers.

The project is designed as a practical DevOps lab to review and reinforce Ansible fundamentals through a realistic multi-server infrastructure automation scenario.

## Project Scenario

A DevOps engineer is responsible for preparing and maintaining multiple Linux servers used to host web applications.

Instead of configuring each server manually over SSH, Ansible is used to define and apply a consistent desired state across all managed nodes.

The current lab contains:

* 1 Ansible Control Node
* 2 Linux Managed Nodes
* SSH key-based authentication
* A dedicated `ansible` automation user
* Centralized inventory management
* Automated baseline server configuration
* Centralized variables
* Ansible Facts and conditions
* Automated Linux user management

## Architecture

```text
                    Ansible Control Node
                            |
                            |
                     SSH / Ansible
                            |
                +-----------+-----------+
                |                       |
                v                       v
             web01                    web02
         192.168.1.20             192.168.1.30
                |                       |
             Ubuntu                  Ubuntu
```

Ansible connects to the managed nodes using the dedicated `ansible` user and performs privileged operations using `become`.

```text
Control Node
     |
     | SSH
     v
ansible user
     |
     | sudo / become
     v
Privileged Tasks
```

